In-Reply-To: <fG2nu24w9Fk.gwHQsehbAwAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <fG2nu24w9Fk.gwHQsehbAwAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/fG2nu24w9Fk/m/8CtbhBxcAwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

iid   group ar1

is the same as

ar1 group iid

so that is for each i_spat_2, you have an ar1 process, and all
ar1'processes are (conditional) indendent.

I guess if you want a 'space time model', you would do

f(i_spat, model='besag', graph=adj_graph, group=i_time,
control.group=list(model='ar1'))

which replace i_spat and i_spat_2 in your formula

