Yes, I remember now that that was implemented after the previous discussion for fmesher. The same technique should be doable for the main INLA call, but the default timeout would need to be essentially infinite.

For fmesher, there is a more practical limit that makes the timeout very rarely needed; unless it ends up in an infinitive loop it will fill memory quite quickly, so the fmesher arguments for limiting the mesh size was added to prevent that. The timeout for fmesher now just prevents the rare infinite loop case.

Finn

