Hello all,

I've recently updated R/Rstudio (R v.4.1.0, Rstudio v.1.4.1717), and I'm getting an error when attempting to install INLA through Rstudio:
> install.packages("INLA", repos=c(getOption("repos"), INLA="inla.r-inla-download.org/R/stable <http://inla.r-inla-download.org/R/stable>"), dep=TRUE)
Installing package into ‘C:/Users/jbaec/Documents/R/win-library/4.1’
(as ‘lib’ is unspecified)
installing the source package ‘INLA’

trying URL 'inla.r-inla-download.org/R/stable/src/contrib/INLA_21.02.23.tar.gz <http://inla.r-inla-download.org/R/stable/src/contrib/INLA_21.02.23.tar.gz>'
 length 169857085 bytes (162.0 MB)
downloaded 21.6 MB

Error in download.file(url, destfile, method, mode = "wb", ...) :
  download from 'inla.r-inla-download.org/R/stable/src/contrib/INLA_21.02.23.tar.gz <http://inla.r-inla-download.org/R/stable/src/contrib/INLA_21.02.23.tar.gz>' failed

So, I also tried the testing version:
> install.packages("INLA",repos=c(getOption("repos"),INLA="https://inla.r-inla-download.org/R/testing"), dep=TRUE)
Installing package into ‘C:/Users/jbaec/Documents/R/win-library/4.1’
(as ‘lib’ is unspecified)
trying URL 'https://inla.r-inla-download.org/R/testing/bin/windows/contrib/4.1/INLA_21.06.11.zip'
 length 96560139 bytes (92.1 MB)
downloaded 18.0 MB

Error in download.file(url, destfile, method, mode = "wb", ...) :
  download from 'https://inla.r-inla-download.org/R/testing/bin/windows/contrib/4.1/INLA_21.06.11.zip' failed

Could anyone advise?

Best,

-Alex B.

